{
  "_help": "Buttons: UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT CROSS CIRCLE SQUARE TRIANGLE L R START SELECT. Values: evdev names (KEY_*, BTN_LEFT/RIGHT/MIDDLE); use + for combinations (KEY_LEFTALT+KEY_TAB). Analog: mode = mouse | keys | none; speed = pixels/s with the stick all the way; curve > 1 = more precision near the center. Old profile names still work: jogo = game, setas = arrows, xbox-ombros = xbox-shoulders.",

  "game": {
    "buttons": {
      "UP": "KEY_W", "DOWN": "KEY_S", "LEFT": "KEY_A", "RIGHT": "KEY_D",
      "CROSS": "KEY_SPACE", "CIRCLE": "KEY_LEFTCTRL", "SQUARE": "KEY_R", "TRIANGLE": "KEY_E",
      "L": "BTN_RIGHT", "R": "BTN_LEFT",
      "START": "KEY_ESC", "SELECT": "KEY_TAB"
    },
    "analog": {"mode": "mouse", "speed": 900, "deadzone": 0.15, "curve": 2.0}
  },

  "desktop": {
    "buttons": {
      "UP": "KEY_UP", "DOWN": "KEY_DOWN", "LEFT": "KEY_LEFT", "RIGHT": "KEY_RIGHT",
      "CROSS": "BTN_LEFT", "CIRCLE": "BTN_RIGHT", "SQUARE": "KEY_ENTER", "TRIANGLE": "KEY_LEFTMETA",
      "L": "KEY_PAGEUP", "R": "KEY_PAGEDOWN",
      "START": "KEY_ESC", "SELECT": "KEY_LEFTALT+KEY_TAB"
    },
    "analog": {"mode": "mouse", "speed": 700, "deadzone": 0.15, "curve": 2.2}
  },

  "_help_xbox": "type gamepad: the PC gets a virtual Xbox 360 controller. Targets: A B X Y LB RB LT RT BACK START GUIDE L3 R3, DPAD_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT, LS_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT and RS_UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT (sticks on digital buttons); + presses more than one. shift: while that button is held, the shift.buttons table applies (anything not in it uses the normal one); a quick tap on it alone is shift.tap. analog.stick = left | right | dpad | none; deadzone and max as a fraction of the travel; digital_stick = how far the stick goes with RS_*/LS_* (1 = all the way).",

